### Kevalon ERP Auth Endpoints HTTP Requests Collection
# This file is compatible with VS Code REST Client extension.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/auth

# Store tokens for downstream request calls in your IDE editor
@accessToken = YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN
@refreshToken = YOUR_REFRESH_TOKEN
@resetToken = YOUR_RESET_PASSWORD_TOKEN
@verificationToken = YOUR_EMAIL_VERIFICATION_TOKEN
@sessionId = YOUR_SESSION_OBJECT_ID

### 1. Register a new user
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Jane Doe",
  "email": "jane.doe@example.com",
  "password": "Password123",
  "phone": "+12025550143"
}


### 2. Login (Without 2FA enabled initially)
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jane.doe@example.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}


### 3. Get profile (/me) - Requires Access Token
GET {{baseUrl}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### 4. Send OTP (For 2FA Setup)
POST {{baseUrl}}/send-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jane.doe@example.com",
  "purpose": "2fa_setup"
}


### 5. Verify OTP (For 2FA Setup)
# Get the 6-digit OTP code printed in the server logs/console and put it here
POST {{baseUrl}}/verify-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jane.doe@example.com",
  "otp": "123456",
  "purpose": "2fa_setup"
}


### 6. Login again (With 2FA enabled now)
# This will return "twoFactorRequired: true" and trigger server-side send-otp
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jane.doe@example.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}


### 7. Verify OTP (For Login)
# Get the 6-digit OTP code printed in the server logs/console and put it here
POST {{baseUrl}}/verify-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jane.doe@example.com",
  "otp": "123456",
  "purpose": "login"
}


### 8. Refresh Token Rotation
POST {{baseUrl}}/refresh-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}


### 9. Request Password Reset Link
POST {{baseUrl}}/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jane.doe@example.com"
}


### 10. Reset Password
# Get the token from the email link printed in the server logs and place here
POST {{baseUrl}}/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{resetToken}}",
  "newPassword": "NewPassword456"
}


### 11. Logout (Invalidates specific token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}


### 12. Verify Email Address
# Get the token from the verification link printed in the server logs/console
POST {{baseUrl}}/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{verificationToken}}"
}


### 13. Resend Verification Email
# Always returns 200 regardless of whether email exists (anti-enumeration)
POST {{baseUrl}}/resend-verification-email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jane.doe@example.com"
}


### 14. List Active Sessions (Device Management)
# Returns all non-revoked, non-expired sessions for the logged-in user
GET {{baseUrl}}/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### 15. Revoke a Specific Session (Remote Logout)
# Use the sessionId returned by GET /sessions
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/sessions/{{sessionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
